"""Editorial question review for prehistoric life and Earth mysteries."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


DINOSAURS = """history_origins|How a Dinosaur Group Was Identified|Which fossils first led researchers to recognize one dinosaur lineage?|Compare dated descriptions, specimens, and later reclassification.
famous_examples|A Famous Fossil Revisited|What does one well-known specimen actually preserve?|Examine collection context, preparation, anatomy, and missing parts.
hidden_stories|The Field Team Behind a Fossil|Who found, excavated, prepared, and studied one specimen?|Use field notes, collection records, credits, and local stewardship.
beginner_explainers|From Bone to Dinosaur Claim|How do scientists infer an extinct animal from fossil remains?|Follow one specimen through geology, identification, comparison, and uncertainty.
advanced_concepts|Reconstructing a Dinosaur's Movement|Which evidence constrains one model of posture or locomotion?|Compare joints, trackways, biomechanical assumptions, and living analogues.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Uncertain Dinosaur Behavior|What evidence could distinguish two explanations of a fossil trace?|Compare preservation, context, analogues, and testable predictions.
technology_innovation|Scanning Changes a Fossil Study|What did one imaging or preparation method reveal without destroying a specimen?|Compare original observation, scan resolution, segmentation, and interpretation.
people_personalities|Revisiting a Paleontologist's Claim|How did one researcher interpret a fossil, and what changed later?|Use original publication, specimen access, and later critique.
major_events|A Find That Revised a Timeline|Which discovery changed the known age or distribution of a dinosaur group?|Check stratigraphy, dating, identification, and independent confirmation.
how_it_works|How a Fossil Is Dated|What evidence dates one dinosaur-bearing layer?|Explain stratigraphic position, datable material, method, and uncertainty.
rise_fall|A Dinosaur Hypothesis Falls Away|Which new fossils or analyses overturned one influential reconstruction?|Compare old and new evidence without mocking earlier work.
then_vs_now|The Same Dinosaur Across Reconstructions|Why does a current depiction differ from an older one?|Compare available fossils, living relatives, methods, and artistic inference.
future_developments|A Fossil Test Still Needed|Which new specimen or analysis could resolve one prehistoric debate?|State predicted evidence, collection ethics, and uncertainty.
myths_vs_facts|A Dinosaur Image Checked|Does a popular depiction match the fossil evidence for its named species?|Separate supported anatomy, close-relative inference, and artistic choice.
documentary_stories|One Fossil's Evidence Trail|How did a specimen move from field discovery to published interpretation?|Build a dated record of provenance, preparation, study, and revision.
observation_to_explanation|A Fossil Trace and Its Maker|How is a track, bite mark, or nest linked to a proposed animal or behavior?|Compare geometry, context, alternatives, and confidence.
measurement_method|Measuring a Dinosaur Fossil|Which dimensions or features underlie one body-size estimate?|Read specimen measurements, scaling model, and error range.
scale_and_timespan|A Site in Deep Time|How do fossils from one formation map onto a long geological interval?|Distinguish layer, absolute age estimate, depositional duration, and later disturbance.
field_vs_lab|A Fossil in Context and Collection|What information is lost or gained when a specimen leaves its excavation site?|Compare field mapping, preparation, imaging, and curation records.
natural_variation|Variation Within a Fossil Species|Are differences among specimens due to age, sex, individual variation, or species?|Compare sample size, preservation, growth markers, and alternative classifications.
mechanism_chain|From Anatomy to Function|Which steps support an inference about feeding or movement?|Separate preserved structure, mechanical model, living analogue, and behavior.
extreme_case|An Unusually Large Specimen|Is one giant fossil typical of its species or a sampling outlier?|Check completeness, scaling, growth stage, and comparative sample.
classification_debate|Where a Dinosaur Species Begins|Do disputed fossils represent one species or several?|Compare diagnostic characters, age, variation, and phylogenetic method.
interacting_systems|A Prehistoric Food Web|How did plants, herbivores, predators, and environment interact at one site?|Use fossils from the same dated formation and account for preservation bias.
data_gap|The Missing Part of the Skeleton|Which absent bones most limit a reconstruction?|Identify preserved elements, related taxa, and uncertainty in inferred anatomy.
prediction_test|A Paleo Model Meets a New Fossil|What did a dated reconstruction predict before another specimen was found?|Compare prediction, new material, and revised interpretation.
human_impact|Fossil Heritage Today|How does collection and display affect source communities and scientific access?|Review ownership, permits, curation, local participation, and research availability.
field_field_sampling|A Fossil Site's Sampling Bias|Which collection choices affect the animals represented in one assemblage?|Map excavated layers, screen size, weathering, and specimen selection.
field_land_use|The Ancient Landscape|What sediment and fossil evidence locates one dinosaur habitat in a river, coast, or plain?|Reconstruct a named formation without equating ancient and modern land use.
field_weather_variability|Ancient Seasonal Conditions|Can growth marks, sediments, or isotopes reveal seasonal variation?|Compare proxy assumptions, dating, and alternative causes.
field_habitat_change|A Habitat Through Layers|How did one prehistoric environment change across a stratigraphic sequence?|Use comparable deposits, fossils, chronology, and sampling effort.
field_restoration_evidence|Evidence Behind a Life Reconstruction|Which features of a museum or film dinosaur are measured and which are restored?|Label fossil-supported anatomy, relative-based inference, and artistic choices."""


EARTH = """history_origins|How an Earth Puzzle Was Solved|Which measurements changed one explanation of a natural phenomenon?|Trace original observations, competing models, and later tests.
famous_examples|A Striking Geological Feature|What evidence explains one famous landform?|Compare mapped rock, process rates, age estimates, and alternative accounts.
hidden_stories|People Who Measured the Landscape|Whose field observations or local knowledge shaped one finding?|Use attributed records and respect community knowledge and permissions.
beginner_explainers|From Clue to Earth Process|How do scientists infer a process from rocks, water, or terrain?|Follow one place from observation through measurement and model.
advanced_concepts|Several Causes of One Landform|How do interacting tectonic, climate, and erosion processes shape a site?|Define timescale and compare evidence for each contributor.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Earth Signal Still Unexplained|Which natural explanations remain for one puzzling observation?|Check measurement quality, competing predictions, and unresolved gaps.
technology_innovation|A Sensor Sees Hidden Change|What did one satellite or field instrument add to a geological investigation?|Compare resolution, coverage, calibration, and ground validation.
people_personalities|A Field Scientist's Changing View|How did a named investigator revise a hypothesis after new evidence?|Use dated publications and records rather than a hero narrative.
major_events|A Natural Event Rewrites a Map|What did one earthquake, eruption, flood, or landslide change?|Compare before-and-after measurements and documented impacts.
how_it_works|How a Geological Hazard Is Monitored|What data feed one monitoring or warning system?|Map instruments, thresholds, uncertainty, communication, and limitations.
rise_fall|A Natural Explanation Rejected|Which new observation ruled out an earlier account?|Compare predictions and measurements at the same site.
then_vs_now|A Landscape Across Two Surveys|What changed in one landform between dated observations?|Use comparable maps, instruments, and weather conditions.
future_developments|The Next Measurement of an Earth Mystery|Which observation could separate two remaining explanations?|Specify instrument, site, timescale, and feasible result.
myths_vs_facts|Checking a Natural-Mystery Claim|Does a viral claim match the geology and measurement record?|Check location, age, image provenance, and alternative causes.
documentary_stories|A Field Investigation's Evidence Trail|How did investigators move from an odd observation to a published explanation?|Build a dated record of fieldwork, analysis, challenge, and revision.
observation_to_explanation|From Pattern to Process|Which assumptions connect an observed Earth pattern to a mechanism?|Check spatial context, timing, alternative processes, and model limits.
measurement_method|Measuring Ground Change|How was motion, depth, chemistry, or age measured at one site?|Read calibration, sampling interval, units, and uncertainty.
scale_and_timespan|Fast Event, Slow Landscape|How does a brief event fit within a longer geological process?|Compare event record, accumulated change, and dating limits.
field_vs_lab|Testing Rock Behavior|Do laboratory results apply to a natural slope or fault?|Compare material, pressure, water, scale, and field validation.
natural_variation|An Anomaly Against Background|Is a striking measurement outside ordinary local variation?|Use baseline, seasonality, sensor error, and historical records.
mechanism_chain|How One Earth Process Unfolds|Which steps link a trigger to observed terrain change?|Separate measured movement, modeled steps, and missing evidence.
extreme_case|An Exceptional Natural Event|Does one record-setting event reveal general risk?|Compare rarity, observation period, physical limits, and exposure.
classification_debate|Naming a Geological Feature|How do definitions change whether one feature is a crater, sinkhole, or landslide?|Compare diagnostic field evidence and alternative classifications.
interacting_systems|Rain, Rock, and Land Cover|How do weather, geology, and land use combine at one site?|Use a bounded event and avoid assigning one cause without evidence.
data_gap|The Missing Instrument or Record|Which absence most limits one Earth-science explanation?|Map coverage, temporal gaps, sample bias, and feasible follow-up.
prediction_test|An Earth Model Meets a New Event|What did a dated model predict about location, timing, or size?|Compare forecast with observation and uncertainty; do not imply precise prediction where impossible.
human_impact|A Natural Process and Local Decisions|How did evidence about one hazard inform planning or response?|Trace public records, affected residents, and measured outcomes.
field_field_sampling|Collecting Ground Evidence|How were rock, soil, or water samples chosen at one site?|Record locations, depth, timing, contamination controls, and permissions.
field_land_use|Land Use Changes the Signal|How did roads, drainage, or clearing alter a measured process?|Compare site history, controls, and natural variation.
field_weather_variability|Weather as a Confounder|Could rain, temperature, or season explain an apparent anomaly?|Use concurrent weather and repeat measurements.
field_habitat_change|Landscape and Ecosystem Together|How did geological change affect a local habitat, or vice versa?|Compare dated terrain and ecological data without assuming one-way cause.
field_restoration_evidence|Did a Landscape Repair Work?|Which measurements show whether one restoration or stabilization effort succeeded?|Compare baseline, reference sites, maintenance, and follow-up period."""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("029", "029_dinosaurs_prehistoric_world", DINOSAURS,
                  "Dinosaur fossils and prehistoric environments through provenance, dating, anatomy, paleoecology, reconstruction, and uncertainty.",
                  "field notes and stratigraphic records, curated specimens and scans, dated paleontology papers, fossil measurements, comparative anatomy, and geological dating studies",
                  "Separate preserved evidence from inference and visual restoration. Verify specimen provenance and collection permissions, name geological age and uncertainty, and avoid treating one fossil as a complete species portrait.")
    revise_domain("030", "030_earth_natural_mysteries", EARTH,
                  "Earth processes and unresolved field observations through measured geology, weather, timescale, alternative explanations, and human decisions.",
                  "geological surveys and maps, calibrated sensor records, field samples and lab analyses, remote sensing, dated hazard notices, and affected community accounts",
                  "Check location, time, calibration, and competing natural processes. Do not convert an unexplained observation into a supernatural conclusion or imply precise hazard prediction.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
